{
  "version": "1.9.4",
  "changelog": "Save-race fixes. (1) Push, the 5-minute auto-push, and the Settings key-saved callback could start two round-trip saves at once; their reads and writes interleaved and GitHub refused the loser with a '…is at X but expected Y' mismatch — the save that failed on 2026-10-16. Now only one save trip runs at a time; extra triggers fold into at most one follow-up trip, and only when the map actually changed during the push. (2) If a push is refused because the file changed between the editor's read and its write (any writer can cause that, not just this app), the editor re-reads the file's current fingerprint once and retries once with the same content. (3) Reopening the editor no longer overwrites locally saved-but-unpushed edits with the fresh download: if this computer holds unpublished changes, the editor loads those, says so in plain language, and keeps them pushable.",
